<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Fitna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/680">680</a>–692</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Fitna was a period of civil war in the Islamic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> from 680 to 692. It began after the accession of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazid-i">Yazid I</a> and included the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husayn-ibn-ali">Husayn ibn Ali</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-karbala">Karbala</a> and the rival caliphate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-allah-ibn-al-zubayr">Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> describe how the Marwanid branch of the Umayyads emerged victorious and consolidated the dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-fitna.jpg" alt="Second Fitna" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: original map by Al Ameer son; SVG version by Konstantinos Plakidas · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Second_Fitna_Territorial_Control_Map_ca_686.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
